      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Multi-solution PnP. A KNOWN pose is projected to 2D, then recovered three ways with 'CV Solve PnP (All Poses)': the generic solver over all six points (one answer), IPPE over the four PLANAR ones (TWO answers - the classic planar flip) and P3P over the same four. Every candidate carries the reprojection error this node computes uniformly, so the lowest one is the physical pose; the two axis previews draw the best candidate and the runner-up so the ambiguity is visible, not just tabulated. The last row feeds two points into the same node: too few for any solver, so it reports found=false with empty stacks instead of raising."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
